.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt VIRTIO-BLK 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm virtio-blk
.Nd virtio block driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/virtio-blk
.Op Ar bar Ns = Ns Ar n
.Op Ar bar_size Ns = Ns Ar bytes
.Op Ar dma Ns = Ns Ar bytes
.Op Ar irq Ns = Ns Ar line
.Op Ar test
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the userspace driver for a modern (virtio 1.0) PCI block function.  It is
launched by
.Xr devd 8
for a function whose vendor and device ids match
.Pa /etc/drivers.toml ,
and receives four handles in the documented order: the device BAR (3), the
function's configuration page (4), a DMA buffer (5) and a legacy interrupt (6).
The command-line arguments are the values
.Nm
gets from
.Xr devd 8 :
.Va bar ,
.Va bar_size ,
.Va dma
and
.Va irq .
.Pp
The driver resets the function, negotiates
.Dv VIRTIO_F_VERSION_1
plus
.Dv VIRTIO_BLK_F_FLUSH
and the read-only feature when the device offers them, and reads the capacity
from the device configuration in 512-byte sectors.  One split request queue of
at most eight entries is programmed in the DMA buffer.  A request is the
bounded chain header, optional data and status; the data window is 65,024
bytes (127 sectors), so a 128-sector protocol request is split into two
chunks.  Every sector range,
descriptor index and used-ring length is checked before it is used.  Completion
is driven by the ISR byte and the transferred interrupt with a bounded wait; a
timeout resets the device and returns
.Er EIO ,
never a partial reply.
.Pp
The driver serves the
.Dq disk:
scheme with the
.Xr blockd 8
framing.  The only device path is
.Dq 0 ,
the whole device.  INFO, READ, WRITE and FLUSH are supported; LIST returns
.Er EINVAL
because partitions are
.Xr blockd 8 Ns 's
job.  A read-only device refuses a writable open and every write with
.Er EROFS .
.Pp
With
.Ar test
the driver also runs the qtest self-test: cycle 1 writes a deterministic
pattern across the data area, flushes, reads a one-mebibyte sample and records
a marker; after a client flush it resets and exits.  Cycle 2 re-reads the whole
data area byte for byte, compares the sample checksum with the marker and
exits.  The production driver (no
.Ar test )
never writes data the client did not ask for.
.Pp
The device must be a modern-only function (for example QEMU's
.Ql virtio-blk-pci,disable-legacy=on ) whose registers live in a memory BAR.
Legacy virtio, MSI and MSI-X are not supported yet; the driver uses the
function's legacy INTx line.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/drivers.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/drivers.toml
the driver table that launches
.Nm
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr blockd 8 ,
.Xr pcid 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
.Sh STANDARDS
Virtio 1.0 (OASIS), PCI Local Bus 3.0.
